From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] casilda: give every mapped toplevel Wayland keyboard focus

casilda_compositor_focus_toplevel() is the only path that calls
wlr_seat_keyboard_notify_enter(), and xdg_toplevel_map() only reached it for
a fresh, plain, non-maximized map. A toplevel that maps maximized or
fullscreen - which is every Sugar Activity filling the compositor viewport -
and a toplevel remapped from saved state both fell through without ever
receiving keyboard focus, so the client's own widgets stayed unfocused until
a pointer click happened to grab focus for them. Keyboard-only interaction
could therefore never reach an Activity.

focus_toplevel() already returns early when the surface is focused or the
toplevel owns child toplevels, so calling it unconditionally is safe.

Upstream candidate: https://gitlab.gnome.org/jpu/casilda

diff --git a/src/casilda-compositor.c b/src/casilda-compositor.c
index 5606b10..fc27289 100644
--- a/src/casilda-compositor.c
+++ b/src/casilda-compositor.c
@@ -2769,8 +2769,14 @@ xdg_toplevel_map (struct wl_listener *listener, G_GNUC_UNUSED void *data)
                                              gtk_widget_get_width (widget),
                                              gtk_widget_get_height (widget));
     }
-  else
-    casilda_compositor_focus_toplevel (toplevel, xdg_toplevel->base->surface);
+
+  /* Grant Wayland keyboard focus regardless of how this toplevel mapped.
+   * A maximized/fullscreen map (the common case for a Sugar Activity
+   * filling the compositor viewport) and a restored-state map previously
+   * fell through without ever calling wlr_seat_keyboard_notify_enter, so
+   * the toplevel's own widgets never saw keyboard focus until a pointer
+   * click first grabbed it. */
+  casilda_compositor_focus_toplevel (toplevel, xdg_toplevel->base->surface);
 
   casilda_compositor_queue_draw (toplevel->priv);
 }
